From 2b64d3d2fe74ecdbf9c7455db282add7a4cd0109 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Sotraidis <56282582+chrissotraidis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 23:27:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] gxcore: the hardware's eight texgens and sixteen TEV stages

Wind Waker's dungeon map draws quads with all eight raw texture coordinates, eight texgens (TEX0..7 in order) and twelve TEV stages. gxcore capped texgens at 5 and stages at 8 (the first-play maximum), so the map showed only its room markers (BlueWake #74).

kMaxTexGens is now the hardware's 8 and kMaxTevStages its 16. The raw coordinates a vertex carries into the fixed decoded layout stay at five (kMaxRawTexCoords; the layout is held by WebGPU's 16 vertex inputs, and a wider layout would cost every vertex). A vertex with TEX5..7 and no normal carries those three in the normal, binormal and tangent slots it doesn't use (ShaderKey::raw_tex_hi_in_nbt, in the old padding byte); both shader generators read them there and the pipeline layout declares the three inputs. Pipeline config version 13.
